.TH MU2EDAQ-RUNLOG-DB 7 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-runlog-db \- web viewer and entry tool for the Mu2e DAQ run log
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B http://<host>:8000/runs/
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Django 4.2 application (project
.BR runlogdb ,
app
.BR runs )
served by gunicorn (production) or
.B manage.py runserver
(development) on TCP port 8000.
It queries the run-log tables
.BR run ,
.BR subrun ,
.BR run_end_info ,
.BR run_type
and their lookups, and offers forms that insert rows into
.BR run ,
.B run_end_info
and
.BR subrun .
.PP
In production the tables live in PostgreSQL and are written by the otsdaq
run-info plugin
.B DBRunInfo
(otsdaq-mu2e,
.IR RunInfoPlugins/DBRunInfo_runInfo.cc ),
which inserts into
.BR run ,
.BR run_transition ,
.B run_end_info
and
.B config
under the schema named by
.BR OTSDAQ_RUNINFO_DATABASE_SCHEMA .
The
.B run
row's number comes from the database sequence
.RB ( "RETURNING run_number" ).
.B DBRunInfo
does not write
.BR subrun .
.SH HTTP ROUTES
.TP
.B GET /
Redirect to
.IR /runs/ .
.TP
.B GET /runs/?start_time=&end_time=
Runs whose
.B create_time
falls in the UTC range.
.TP
.B GET /runs/<N>/subruns/
Subruns of run
.I N
with total events and end info.
.TP
.B GET /runs/subruns/ewt/?ewt_min=&ewt_max=
Subruns whose
.RB [ min_ewt ,
.BR max_ewt ]
contains or overlaps the given Event Window Tag range.
.TP
.B GET /runs/entry/
Index of the entry forms.
.TP
.B GET|POST /runs/entry/run/
Insert a
.B run
row with an operator-supplied run number.
.TP
.B GET|POST /runs/entry/run\-end/
Insert a
.B run_end_info
row.
.TP
.B GET|POST /runs/entry/subrun/
Insert a
.B subrun
row.
.TP
.B GET|POST /runs/bug\-report/
Create a GitHub issue in
.B github.repo
with the server's token.
.TP
.B GET /runs/about/
About page; the only
.I /runs/
route without
.BR @login_required .
.TP
.B /accounts/...
django-allauth: login, logout, signup, social login callbacks.
.TP
.B /admin/
Django admin; the run-log models are not registered, only Django's and allauth's.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.TP
.B auth.enabled: false
(development overlay, and the default for every launch through the start
scripts).
Every request is logged in as superuser
.BR dev ,
including
.IR /admin/ .
.TP
.B auth.enabled: true
(production overlay).
Every view above except the about page requires a login.
The sign-in page shows only the Fermilab and Google buttons, but the
allauth username/password signup endpoint
.I /accounts/signup/
accepts a POST from anyone, logs the new user in, and grants the same read
and write access as an SSO user.
Any Google account is also accepted.
There is no authorisation layer: every authenticated user can use the entry
forms and the bug-report page.
.PP
Sessions are database-backed (Django default).
Nothing sets HTTPS, HSTS or secure-cookie options.
.SH DISCOVERY
When serving,
.I runs/apps.py
starts a
.B mu2edaq_discovery.Responder
(name
.BR "Run Log Database" ,
app
.BR runlog\-db ,
port
.BR RUNLOGDB_PORT ,
scheme
.BR http ,
no
.BR meta )
if the optional package is importable.
It advertises the host's FQDN even when the server is bound to 127.0.0.1.
Under gunicorn each worker process starts its own responder.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I runlogdb/settings.py
Settings loader; see
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5).
.TP
.I runlogdb/db_router.py
Returns
.B allow_migrate=False
for the
.B runs
app on PostgreSQL; it does not route or restrict reads or writes.
.TP
.I db\-schema.md
Entity-relationship diagram of the production schema.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh (1),
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR manage.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5)
